Adds a dedicated /refund-policy page covering Axis subscription billing —
required by Paddle (our merchant of record) as part of account
verification, alongside the existing Terms of Service and Privacy Policy
pages.

- src/legacy-pages/RefundPolicy.tsx: page content, following the same
  structure/styling as TermsOfService.tsx and PrivacyPolicy.tsx. Covers
  the 7-day free trial, refund eligibility windows for monthly vs annual
  plans, cancellation instructions, and how to request a refund.
- src/app/(public)/refund-policy/page.tsx: thin route wrapper, matching
  the existing /terms and /privacy pattern
- src/components/Footer.tsx: added a 'Refund Policy' link next to
  Terms of Service and Privacy Policy in the footer, so it's
  discoverable site-wide
- src/app/sitemap.ts: registered /refund-policy alongside /privacy
  and /terms

Note: the legacy Supabase edge function sitemap generator
(supabase/functions/sitemap/index.ts) uses different slugs
(/privacy-policy, /terms-of-service) than the actual Next.js routes.
Left as-is since it predates this change and its purpose/status
wasn't clear — worth a follow-up look.

Verified: tsc --noEmit and next build both pass clean; /refund-policy
prerenders as a static page alongside /privacy and /terms.
